The chat's model from the search API's setting

The chat page sends a model with every question, "cesnet/agentic" unless someone
picked another in the model selector, which is off unless the build sets
VITE_SHOW_MODEL_SELECTOR=true. The search API then uses that model, not its own
DEFAULT_LLM_MODEL; a deployment without a CESNET key gets "Missing credentials"
on every chat (staging 2026-11-12, @weber). Send the model only when the selector
is on, so that otherwise the search API's setting chooses it.

- api.ts, sendChatMessage: `model` in the request only with the selector on; the
  argument stays, for the analytics events that name it.
- api.test.ts: without the selector the request has no model; with it, the one
  picked.

